  succession of local branches.

## Closure test

A proposed mechanism must yield, for **any** sufficiently large triangle-free
minimizer A of cardinality n and diameter D, a unit-separated n-point planar
configuration A-prime with diameter strictly below D. All labels, actual diameter
pairs, and initially inactive pair constraints must be accounted for. Comparison
configurations may replace the entire source and need not preserve its contacts.

## Diverse global portfolio

| Mechanism | Exact proposed bridge | Current issue |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Finite conformal reembedding | Normalize a whole-source inversion to minimum distance one and certify a smaller diameter using every pair | Infinitesimal conformal work is already neutralized by canonical stress-midpoint equality; finite improvement has not been shown |
| Rank escape and planar return | Use the negative spectrum of the full signed stress to find a global replacement, then realize it in the plane | A lower weighted diameter energy or a higher-dimensional competitor is insufficient |
| Collective remeshing | Replace all incompatible boundary and interior grains at once; count a full n-point strict-sub-D packet | Density alone allows triangle-free near-optima; integer population and strict diameter must both be paid |
| Global stability of attainment | Exploit exact attainment, rather than a uniform triangle-free density deficit | The triangle-free class is open at each finite source and its infimum may equal D(n) without attaining it |
| Curvature and terminal rigidity | Relate the complete boundary-pinned contact geometry to a full-source capacity bound | Lattice-only component estimates do not control nonlattice macroscopic components |

None of these entries is a proved bridge or a canonical frontier change. Numerical
experiments may reject a bridge but cannot certify global optimality on their own.

## Immediate work

The first exact checkpoint is
`docs/reports/global_separable_distortion_obstruction_2026-10-12.md` and its
verifier. Equal contact/diameter vertex marginals block every positive separable
distance scaling, hence every finite-source Möbius map. An unbounded quadratic
population of triangle-free contact isolates can coexist with this certificate;
the constructed sources nevertheless admit independent strict planar replacements
and are proved nonglobal. Formal improving factors need not be planar realizable.

The next checkpoint is
`docs/reports/global_joint_stress_strain_phase_mechanism_2026-10-12.md`.
A positive stress-only laminate can have isotropic mean, so missing contact
directions alone are compatible. Adding a compatible opening strain in the same
material frame yields strictly negative cross-phase products. Exact periodic
joint fields then have one phase; explicit error/transition/boundary-work bounds
quantify the obstruction. This is a proved formal candidate, not a source theorem.
An exact independently rotated two-phase laminate is jointly compatible with
constant positive stress. Thus the fixed-frame theorem cannot itself exclude
the global multi-grain phase; actual unit-distance source geometry must add
information. Do not shrink the mission to a fixed supplied orientation.

Next: test the **whole-source** material-chart extraction. Grain rotations,
dislocations, unbounded normalized strains, vanishing stress/opening products,
and seam/boundary work must be carried into a global ledger. A chart supplied for
one smaller branch cannot satisfy the extraction obligation. A successful
extraction must still force a unit triangle or a strict n-point planar competitor.
The global closure test and Level I status are unchanged.
